<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12067" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cuspis</span></b> , ĭdis, f.
		etym. dub., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a point, the pointed end</i> of any thing (freq.,
			esp. in the poets). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Prop.: asserum, * <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 2, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vomeris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 18, 48, § 172</span></i>
			. acuta contorum, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 5, 208</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acuta teli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 470</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hastae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.
					5, 9</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">6, 78: jaculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 7, 673</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medicata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 197</span></i>
			: aquilae, <i>the pointed end of the
			standard;</i> Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στύραξ</span>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Caes. 62</span></i> et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b> (pars pro toto). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A spear, javelin, lance</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 11,
				41</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 386</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4,
				6, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. S. 2, 1, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
				673</span></i>; Liv 4, 38, 3 and 4; 8, 7, 9 and 11; <i><span class="en">Plin.
				34, 15, 45, § 152 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A spit</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 14,
				221, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>The trident of Neptune</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				580</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">triplex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 12, 594</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 2,
			181</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<i>The sting of a bee</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21,
				13, 45, § 78</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<i>A scorpion's sting</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				199</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>F.</b>
			<i>A pointed tube</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 8, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
